Issue description
`runHostedCase` currently sends caught errors without an OAuth error code into `assessHostedCase`, whose outcome logic treats a missing code as an allowed result. This allows failed requests and invalid non-OAuth responses to make expected-success fixtures pass.
Fix Focus Areas
- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[300-304]
- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[315-319]
Recommended Fix
Represent caught exceptions as an explicit failed outcome rather than deriving their outcome from an absent OAuth error code. Update `assessHostedCase` or add a dedicated failure-result path so any exception always produces `status: "failed"`, while preserving the redacted error message.
```

