          "body": "Using only `errorCode` to infer rejection means every code-less exception is classified as allowed. I reproduced an `expected: { outcome: "allowed" }` case whose registration throws `Error("offline")`; the result still has `status: "passed"`, so operational failures must fail independently of the expected OAuth outcome.

<details><summary>Technical details</summary>

````markdown
# Do not treat exceptions as allowed authorization outcomes

## Affected sites
- `mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts:300` — exceptions are converted into an optional code plus message.
- `mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts:315` — absence of a code is interpreted as an allowed protocol outcome.

## Required outcome
- Any exception from registration, request dispatch, response parsing, or fixture validation produces `status: "failed"`.
- Only an observed protocol response should be compared with `expected.outcome`.
````

