13\. Insecure callbacks pass regression tests <code>🐞 Bug</code> <code>⛨ Security</code>

<pre>
<b><i>runHostedCase</i></b> extracts a code from the authorization <b><i>Location</i></b> header without checking that the
redirect URI and returned state match <b><i>fixture.authorization</i></b>. A server that sends an authorization
code to a different callback, or drops or changes state, is exchanged and reported as a successful
hosted authorization flow.
</pre>


<details>
<summary><strong>Agent Prompt</strong></summary>

```
Issue description
The hosted authorization runner trusts any `Location` header with a code and does not verify that it targets the requested callback or reflects the supplied state. This permits unsafe authorization callback behavior to be certified by the regression suite.
Fix Focus Areas
- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[237-256]
- mcpfn/testing/src/host-authorization.ts[350-353]
Recommended Fix
Parse the successful authorization redirect and require its origin, path, and relevant query behavior to match the fixture redirect URI, then require its `state` parameter to exactly equal the fixture state before extracting the code. Return a failed result for a mismatch.
```

