P1: A thrown transport/HTTP error during an expected-`allowed` case is reported as `status: "passed"`. The catch block derives `code` from `redactOAuthValue(error)`, which never surfaces a plain Error's `code` (redactError returns only `name`/`message`/`stack`), so `errorCode` is undefined and `assessHostedCase` computes `observedOutcome = "allowed"`, matching the allowed expectation. Reaching this requires only a non-JSON error body (e.g. a 500 token response triggers `throw new Error("Token request returned HTTP 500")`), so genuine endpoint failures can pass silently. Treat catch-block failures as failures regardless of the expected outcome.

