          "body": "This permanently memoizes the first rejected cleanup, while `McpFnClient.cleanupAttempt(true)` retains the failed handle specifically for a later close/reconnect retry. Because the lease also memoizes its rejected `releasePromise`, one transient `revoke` or `dispose` failure leaves every subsequent cleanup returning the same rejection and bricks that client.

