          "outdated": true,
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3991101847",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Reject empty credential header values**\n\nLibrary callers can supply an empty or whitespace-only credential header even though the CLI rejects empty credentials. `Headers` normalizes such a value to `\"\"`, which is added to `secrets`; subsequent redaction evaluates `text.split(\"\").join(\"[REDACTED]\")` for every report string, massively expanding and corrupting the report and potentially causing a successful suite to become truncated or throw at the size cap. Reject empty normalized header values, or at minimum never register an empty value as a secret.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
