          "outdated": true,
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3995312694",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Preserve report keys while redacting credentials**\n\nThe new blank-value guard still accepts nonempty credentials such as `target`, `results`, or `testing`, but this recursion applies substring replacement to object keys as well as values. Such credentials rename fixed report fields—for example, `target` becomes `[REDACTED]`—so target-suite JSON no longer matches its declared schema and JUnit generation can throw while accessing `report.target.kind` or `safe.results`. Redact credential occurrences in values and untrusted payload keys without rewriting the fixed report envelope.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
