        {
          "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-12T05:49:22Z",
          "outdated": true,
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3995312696",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Scrub authenticated runner output-directory artifacts**\n\nWhen authenticated conformance is combined with `outputDir`/`--output-dir`, the official child still writes files directly to the caller-selected directory. If the protected target reflects the opaque credential in a failing response or diagnostic, those child-produced artifacts bypass `redactRemoteCredential`, which only sanitizes the returned result after the process exits; the stdout and `--report` fix therefore does not protect the output directory. Stage and redact these files before exposing them, or reject `outputDir` for authenticated runs.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6hvRyg",
      "isOutdated": false,
      "path": "mcpfn/client/src/client.ts",
      "line": 1028,
      "originalLine": 868,
      "commentsPageInfo": {
        "hasNextPage": false,
        "endCursor": "REDACTED"
      },
      "comments": [
        {
          "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-12T10:15:58Z",
          "outdated": false,
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3995915243",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Retain handles whose credential cleanup fails**\n\nWhen an authenticated target's protocol closes remotely, or an in-progress open is aborted, the client calls this helper with `strict=false` and then discards the only handle reference. If the credential provider's `revoke` or `dispose` rejects, this catch silently consumes the failure; despite the authenticated handle resetting its close promise for a retry, no later `client.close()` can reach it, and the remote-close path even reports cleanup as succeeded. Preserve the handle for retry or retry credential cleanup before swallowing the transport-close error.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
