          "body": "<!-- cubic:v=af62c06d-a138-4c4d-9e49-6f4e5a3f5aa8 -->\n<!-- cubic:review-run=2794c884-4528-5630-ad81-9c892ab7aad2 -->\n<!-- metadata:{\"confidence\":5} -->\nP2: When a library caller acquires credentials from an env var and calls runAuthenticatedOfficialConformance without setting sensitiveEnvironmentVariables (defaults to []), the spawned @modelcontextprotocol/conformance npx process inherits that env var, since buildOfficialConformanceEnvironment only strips explicitly listed names. The CLI wires this correctly, but the library API offers no automatic guard. Note in the credential/headers doc that the credential env must also be listed in sensitiveEnvironmentVariables, or strip credential-source env names automatically.\n\n"
