          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Avoid expanding reports for short credential values**\n\nWhen a valid custom credential is a short common value such as `\"a\"` or `\"1\"`, replacing every substring with the ten-character marker can multiply the serialized report size and turn an otherwise successful near-cap suite into a truncated, `ok: false` report. The fresh evidence beyond the prior blank-value issue is that header validation now rejects only whitespace, so nonempty one-character credentials still reach this replacement loop; use non-expanding masking or otherwise handle short values without corrupting artifact sizing.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
