          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Stop internal retries after handle cleanup fails**\n\nWhen `connectRetries` is nonzero, initialization fails, and closing the authenticated handle cannot revoke its credential, this non-strict cleanup retains but suppresses the failure. `handleInitializationFailure()` then returns normally and `connectInternal()` opens its next attempt, bypassing the public `connect()` guard and acquiring another credential while the previous one remains active. The fresh evidence after retaining failed cleanup is that the internal retry loop never checks `pendingCleanup`; make this cleanup strict or stop retries until it succeeds.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
