          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Scrub opaque credentials before truncating strings**\n\nWhen a payload string is near the 262,144-character limit and generic redaction expands an earlier fragment (for example, replacing `token=x`), `redactOAuthValue` can truncate through a later opaque credential before `scrub` searches for that exact value. The remaining credential prefix no longer matches the registered secret and can therefore leak into authenticated inspect or test artifacts. The fresh evidence beyond the earlier reflected-credential issue is this truncation-before-exact-redaction ordering; replace known credential values before any length-changing redaction or truncation.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
