          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r3998837860",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Track tokens from custom authorization schemes**\n\nWhen a supported custom credential uses a scheme other than Bearer or Basic, such as `Authorization: Token opaque-123`, only the full header value is registered as a secret. If the target reflects the parsed token as `{ \"echo\": \"opaque-123\" }`, the inner value survives report, inspect, and conformance redaction. The fresh evidence beyond the earlier opaque API-key finding is that the new extraction explicitly handles only Bearer and Basic despite exposing `custom` credentials; either capture token components for other schemes or let providers identify the opaque values that must be scrubbed.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
