        {
          "author": "chatgpt-codex-connector",
          "createdAt": "2026-09-15T03:47:11Z",
          "outdated": false,
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4011736872",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Honor the configured authorization-code fixture**\n\nWhen a caller sets `fixture.token.code` to exercise an invalid, expired, or independently authored authorization code, the runner ignores it and always submits the code returned by the authorization redirect. Such a negative token-exchange fixture can therefore pass while never testing its configured input; use the token-request fixture's `code` when supplied, or remove the public field so it cannot silently misconfigure an experiment.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iYHEW",
      "isOutdated": false,
      "path": "mcpfn/inspector/src/index.ts",
