          "createdAt": "2026-09-15T04:55:21Z",
          "outdated": false,
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4012054645",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Substitute placeholders in redacted property keys**\n\nWhen an opaque target credential appears as a property key in operation arguments or returned structured content, payload-mode redaction replaces that key with `${MCPFN_SECRET}`. However, `collectVariables()` examines only object values, and `resolveScenarioVariables()` also preserves keys while substituting values, so the exported scenario omits the required variable and later replays or compares the literal placeholder key instead of the original key. Include object keys in variable discovery and substitution so these exports remain runner-compatible.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iZrJG",
      "isOutdated": true,
      "path": "mcpfn/client/src/client.ts",
