          "createdAt": "2026-09-15T06:35:47Z",
          "outdated": true,
          "url": "https://github.com/21nCo/super-functions/pull/170#discussion_r4012689191",
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Redact client event payloads in payload mode**\n\nWhen an authenticated target's credential equals a protected envelope value, `this.redact(payload)` applies the target's default `preserveKeys: true` behavior to the standalone payload. For example, an API key of `passed` remains visible in a notification payload `{ status: \"passed\" }` because that value is exempted as a root report status, so listeners, inspector snapshots, and suite artifacts can expose the credential. Pass payload mode explicitly while continuing to reconstruct the client-event envelope.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "PRRT_kwDOP-e7KM6iZrJL",
