          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Scrub credential values from authenticated conformance output**\n\nWhen a protected loopback server reflects an opaque credential in a response that the official runner prints—commonly in diagnostics for a failing scenario—the acquired header values are never supplied to the output redactor before this result is returned. `redactOAuthValue` recognizes credential-shaped fields and strings but not an arbitrary API-key value under a field such as `echo`, so the secret can reach the returned report, CLI stdout/stderr, and `--report`; scrub the lease's header values from the conformance result before returning it.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
