          "originalLine": 127,
          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Redact acquired credential values from artifacts**\n\nWhen an authenticated target reflects an opaque credential under a non-sensitive field and a scenario assertion fails, the actual response is embedded in the scenario error, but the acquired header values are never supplied to the redactor. For example, an API key returned as `{ \"echo\": \"opaque-123\" }` survives `redactOAuthValue` and is subsequently written to the JSON/JUnit output and CI artifacts. Track the acquired credential values and replace them explicitly before producing diagnostics or reports.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
