          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Release leases when credential inspection fails**\n\nWhen a JavaScript credential provider returns a malformed credential such as `{ headers: undefined }`, `credentialValues()` throws here after acquisition but before execution enters the `try` block that calls `release()`. The provider's acquired token is consequently never revoked or disposed. Unlike the already-covered cleanup-rejection path, cleanup is not attempted at all; validate or inspect the credential inside a guarded block that releases the lease on every failure.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
