          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Wire authenticated targets into programmatic redaction**\n\nWhen `authenticatedHttpTarget` is used through the public `McpFnInspector` or `McpFnClient` APIs rather than the CLI or target-suite wrapper, this module-private credential state is never consulted. A server that reflects an opaque header value in an ordinary field such as a tool description, result, or logging event will therefore have that value preserved by the inspector's generic `redactOAuthValue()` calls and exposed by `snapshot()`, `exportScenario()`, or diagnostic listeners, despite those programmatic surfaces being documented as redacted. Expose a target-aware redaction hook to the client/inspector or have those surfaces apply the exact credential scrubber while the lease is active.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
