          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Keep credentials registered through failed-open reporting**\n\nWhen a provider supplies an invalid header whose `Headers` validation error contains the raw value (Node does this for multiline values), the target releases the lease before rethrowing, and this block removes the credential from the target redactor. `McpFnClient.openTargetAttempt()` subsequently emits the failed-open diagnostic with that error message, so a direct programmatic client without a `beginTargetCredentialRedaction()` report scope exposes the credential to diagnostic listeners. Fresh evidence beyond the existing live-artifact issue is this post-release failed-open path; retain the secret until the error is sanitized or its diagnostic has been emitted.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
