          "body": "**<sub><sub>![P1 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P1-orange?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Scrub authenticated runner output-directory artifacts**\n\nWhen authenticated conformance is combined with `outputDir`/`--output-dir`, the official child still writes files directly to the caller-selected directory. If the protected target reflects the opaque credential in a failing response or diagnostic, those child-produced artifacts bypass `redactRemoteCredential`, which only sanitizes the returned result after the process exits; the stdout and `--report` fix therefore does not protect the output directory. Stage and redact these files before exposing them, or reject `outputDir` for authenticated runs.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎."
